1: {'E': 7.5, 'P': 8.4, 'L': 7.8, 'E_Expl': 'The speaker establishes credibility by thanking the host and acknowledging the importance of the debate.', 'P_Expl': 'The speaker evokes empathy by focusing on the concerns of Main Street Americans who are struggling.', 'L_Expl': 'The speaker provides logical proposals for protecting taxpayers and addressing the root of economic problems.', 'E_Clauses': {'1': 'Well, thank you very much, Jim, and thanks to the commission and the University of Mississippi, Ole Miss, for hosting us tonight.'}, 'P_Clauses': {'1': 'And although we’ve heard a lot about Wall Street, those of you on Main Street I think have been struggling for a while, and you recognize that this could have an impact on all sectors of the economy.', '2': 'And you’re wondering, how’s it going to affect me? How’s it going to affect my job? How’s it going to affect my house? How’s it going to affect my retirement savings or my ability to send my children to college?'}, 'L_Clauses': {'1': 'So we have to move swiftly, and we’ve got to move wisely.', '2': 'And I’ve put forward a series of proposals that make sure that we protect taxpayers as we engage in this important rescue effort.', '3': 'Number one, we’ve got to make sure that we’ve got oversight over this whole process; $700 billion, potentially, is a lot of money.', '4': 'Number two, we’ve got to make sure that taxpayers, when they are putting their money at risk, have the possibility of getting that money back and gains, if the market — and when the market returns.', '5': 'Number three, we’ve got to make sure that none of that money is going to pad CEO bank accounts or to promote golden parachutes.', '6': 'And, number four, we’ve got to make sure that we’re helping homeowners, because the root problem here has to do with the foreclosures that are taking place all across the country.'}}
